[thin] These picks surround the beveled beverage outlet and the open display pocket at the end of the tip. Lint reports short diagonal chords of 1.146 and 1.366 mm at the pocket corners; the nearest exact faces have local inward chords of 2.4849 and 5.3566 mm at the first picks. The named faces and readings are in ../vent-qualification/centered-layout-lint-review.json. They retain the tube outlet and hardware insertion clearance. These local readings do not qualify the complete rim, printed finish or resistance to damage.
alternatives: Filling inward reduces tube or display clearance. Growing the outside changes the matching display-cover envelope and outlet face. Rounding the pocket corner uses the same hardware clearance and requires a separate insertion review.
