[thin] These are the curved neck and male-plug walls around the shared upper tube/ribbon passage. The saved mesh reports 2.207–2.209 mm at the named locations. Their surfaces retain the arc-guided joint, its slip clearance and the continuous passage. Local geometric thickness does not establish joint strength or endurance.
alternatives: Growing the plug reduces its socket clearance or requires a larger matching base. Filling the passage reduces tube/ribbon clearance. Increasing the outside neck requires a coordinated change to the tip and display cover.
