[slope] This is the rear end of the open display-component channel at S47.24. It bounds the hardware insertion clearance. In the tip's -105 degree print pose, the joint end faces the bed, the crown is raised and this channel-end face points upward. Preserve the opening and remove any adjacent support through the display opening or neck joint before loading hardware; physical removal and contact finish remain print observations.
alternatives: Filling or sloping this boundary changes the matching component insertion envelope. Opening it farther removes the display pocket's end wall. Retain the hardware clearance and inspect supported contacts before loading the display.
