[thin] Outside the cooling/display-seat revision: these retained outlet, pocket and neck surfaces keep their separate thickness findings. The raised bearing pads have a 3.25 x 3.00 mm footprint and 3.50 mm depth; their inner faces meet the channel at X=+/-6.75 mm. The post-publication reading has no step, ledge, skin or fin findings. Short-ray results below the generic 3 mm threshold remain visible in the surface record and do not establish a complete wall minimum or strength. Derek was told existing thin-section findings are separate from this change. See ../../../faucet/sculpted/prints/2026-10-17-localized-cooling-display-clearance-mark2/surface-review.json.
alternatives: Reconcile any retained outlet/rim feature in a dedicated geometry revision with its tube, display and cover clearances. Increasing all stock changes those retained interfaces; physical assembly success does not settle the local geometry question.
